    "not_admission_contract": true,
    "line": "Ordinary signed-size integer coordinates with representable difference/error arithmetic and addressable bounded outputs; exact Bresenham traversal/endpoints. Python conversion/protocol errors preserve source boundary.",
    "rectangle": "Ordinary integer or finite real geometry after literal rounding/clipping; owned dynamic-rank meshgrid coordinate generation, default xy first-two-axis swap. Do not flatten documented output.",
    "disk_ellipse": "Ordinary finite f64 geometry and prepared literal bounding box/scalar NumPy modulo+trig; own strict-distance classification and ordered coordinate compaction. Initial other dtype/protocol/nonfinite and exceptional-FP routes remain explicit providers until proven; no blanket libm parity claim.",
